        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43420</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43420"/>
        <updated>2026-03-12T23:37:17.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/217326?u=a4cdaefc3a39658f4d104b96ec8c78f10ac63d12&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h2 dir="auto">Summary</h2>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Add a new guide page (<code class="notranslate">Web/Performance/Guides/bfcache</code>) explaining the back/forward cache</li>
<li>Covers: how bfcache works, bfcache vs HTTP caching (RFC 9111 Section 6), stale content handling via <code class="notranslate">pageshow</code>, what blocks bfcache (unload, no-store, open connections), monitoring with <code class="notranslate">notRestoredReasons</code>, and best practices</li>
<li>Links the guide from the Performance landing page and the bfcache glossary entry</li>
</ul>
<h2 dir="auto">Motivation</h2>
<p dir="auto">The bfcache glossary entry is brief and doesn't cover how bfcache interacts with HTTP caching, what blocks it, or how to handle stale content. A maintainer requested a full guide page under Web/Performance.</p>
<p dir="auto">As requested in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3433247968" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41211" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/41211/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41211">#41211</a>.</p>
<h2 dir="auto">Test plan</h2>
