    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Technical review: Document customizable select listboxes]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43352</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43352"/>
        <updated>2026-03-11T16:35:55.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Chrome has supported <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Extensions/Forms/Customizable_select" rel="nofollow">Customizable <code class="notranslate">&lt;select&gt;</code> elements</a> (via <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/appearance#base-select" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">appearance: base-select</code></a>) for single dropdown selects since version 135, and since 145, now supports it for listbox selects, e.g. <code class="notranslate">&lt;select size="3"&gt;</code> or <code class="notranslate">&lt;select multiple&gt;</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto">See <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/6222145025867776" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6222145025867776</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR does a few things:</p>
<ol dir="auto">
<li>Adds a separate guide covering customizable select listboxes. I felt that the existing customizable select elements guide was long enough already, plus the listbox variant has some differences in intent and implementation that are worth calling out separately.
<ul dir="auto">
<li>This one contains a few examples that could do with checking for accessibility, UX, suitability, etc. I ran with the idea of creating some complex/unusual listbox examples to show what is now possible, and I am hoping I didn't get too carried away.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Updates the existing customizable select elements guide to correct the information about listboxes not being supported, which is now wrong, and adds decent coverage of using <code class="notranslate">&lt;optgroup&gt;</code> in customizable selects (this was previously glossed over).</li>
<li>Updates nav menus to fit the new guide into the forms module sequence.</li>
<li>Updates a few other articles to fix/add mentions as required.</li>
</ol>

<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>

<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #43339.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4022290609" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43339" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43339/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43339">#43339</a></p>



]]></content>
